{"id": "EUVD-2026-86927", "enisaUuid": "08393f0b-774f-3aa1-8b3d-d660c1df1e28", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntipc: Dont send random pad bytes in RESET/ACTIVATE messages\n\nThe interface name is passed in a fixed length (TIPC_MAX_IF_NAME) buffer.\nReplace the strcpy(data, l->if_name) with memcpy() so that the\npad bytes are actually written (l->if_name[] is zero padded)\nrather than sending random bytes from the skb to the remote system.\n\nReplace two other strcpy() with strscpy().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dbb628cfc592a4148d8136dcda1f706cdcad4f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48033a89356b8ae21a94db70c79bb6fcc91a23c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ab2977323d5f068a872126f7818d1aeb9e9ca0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bee1459e57f2e0bd240c62f35c0a284291e27971", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81c600c26302a27852ed8b19c5f2f647ea3555c9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98097", "GHSA-3hxh-h963-cm8c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1fb10924-3ce7-3f5a-a9f2-b16a9063310e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e74a386d70c793ef44678b44b021c99094b28c47 <bee1459e57f2e0bd240c62f35c0a284291e27971"}, {"id": "31e1d861-6f86-3573-83fa-07c948a2a6df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "336d41cf-708e-3efe-b273-9cbc5ab58aa2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e74a386d70c793ef44678b44b021c99094b28c47 <81c600c26302a27852ed8b19c5f2f647ea3555c9"}, {"id": "40e0429b-681e-3984-b819-ef335651505c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e74a386d70c793ef44678b44b021c99094b28c47 <48033a89356b8ae21a94db70c79bb6fcc91a23c2"}, {"id": "45ffef4f-dcff-33a7-bbf5-b39881ad5769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "ven